{{also|nudel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Attested since 16th century, further origin {{unk|de|title=unknown}}. Perhaps from {{bor|de|szl|knudel|t=dumpling, noodle}}, from {{der|de|gml|knudel}}, {{m|gml|knūdel}} (compare {{cog|gmh|knödel|t=dumpling, noodle}}); or from {{bor|de|vls|noedel}}, a variant of {{m|vls|knoedel}}, {{m|vls|knuddel|t=dumpling}}, all related to {{cog|nds-de|Knudel|t=lump, mass}}, {{cog|de|Knödel|t=dumpling}}, {{cog|nl|knoedel|t=dumpling, noodle}}.<ref>{{R:de:EWbD|Nudel}}</ref> Later Dutch {{m|nl|noedel}} is a borrowing from the German.

Alternatively, perhaps from {{bor|de|lld|menudli|t=small piece of dough found in soup}}, from {{der|de|la|minutulus}}, diminutive of {{m|la|minūtus|t=diminished, diminutive, lessened}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈnuːdəl/|[ˈnuːdl̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Nudel.ogg|Audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Nudel.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Nudeln|Nüdelchen}}

# a [[noodle]], a string or lump of [[pasta]]
# {{lb|de|in the plural}} [[pasta]]
# {{lb|de|in compounds}} certain other kinds of [[pastry|pastries]]
# {{lb|de|informal}} a [[person]], usually [[female]], who is [[funny]] and [[cheerful]], especially when also having a pleasantly [[plump]], [[buxom]] figure

